T|fknrtd doctor with defaultBaseRef=main => 'main resolves to a commit.'
B|FIXED IN THE AUDIT SEAT: the base-branch check interpolated an empty defaultBaseRef into its own message, printing a headless '√ Base branch resolves   resolves to a commit.' and naming something other than the ref it probed. It now names HEAD explicitly and tells the reader to set defaultBaseRef. A self-test covers the unset case and asserts the detail never opens headless.
Q|The wording fix was made by the auditing seat rather than a repair round, at the user's explicit direction, so that one hunk had no independent reviewer.
